              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "карман (karmán) — Old Russian already had the name Kormanŭ. Turkic karman, \"a pocket, a purse\", was once taken as the source; Radloff saw it as a loan from Russian, and Räsänen again argued for a Turkic origin (Vasmer)."
            }
